## Method and limits

The supplied Prism result has no observation window or end date; the gap to today, 2026-10-23, cannot be calculated. It reports both claims in the intersection lane and provides no match-mode details or coverage dates [c1]. The CSV marks coverage partial because the call reports selected aggregate fields, not a paper-level export.

“Papers-both-poles” and subject/outcome counts are corpus metadata. Corpus-mix counts are Prism’s stance categories; document-read counts are a separate field and should not be added to or substituted for the corpus mix. Neither is a count of job losses, wage increases, or necessarily independent studies. The comparison’s verdict that the second claim has more evidence is Prism’s interpretation of its reported volumes [c1]. The ratio and difference above are arithmetic derived from those volumes. The supplied data cannot establish causal effect sizes, evidence quality across the full corpus, or whether wage gains occur without employment losses in a particular jurisdiction.

